{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LVFZYV2hss1kn2mXQcVycy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Nightly Sweep System â€” Execution Plan (v4)\n2\t**Project codename:** *Aurora* (Always-on Understanding of Research, Operations, and Reasoning Agents)\n3\t**Author:** drafted with John Â· v1 2026-05-15 (initial) Â· v2 2026-05-15 (post deep-think/deep-research review) Â· v3 2026-05-15 (decisions locked in Â§17) Â· v4 2026-05-18 (post-launch reconciliation: Â§18 status, Â§19 GWL/OpenClaw integration scope, Â§20 next-steps punch list) Â· **v4.1 2026-05-18 PM (audit-driven reconciliation: 4 parallel audit subagents verified every Â§18 + Â§18.3 claim against the live install; Â§18.2 extended with 13 new gaps the doc had missed, Â§18.3 corrected on the Gemini-CLI install false claim, Â§20 fully re-prioritized into a 22-item plan; Â§21 audit stamp added)** Â· **v4.2 2026-05-19 (overnight delta in Â§18.2.quater: skills+tools sweeps ok, agents sweep hard-failed on Anthropic 529 Overloaded; KB to 356 artifacts; CHANGELOG total-drift widened; publisher slot drifted to 08:30; Bucket A-D items resolved or partially-resolved are stamped in Â§20)** Â· **v4.3 2026-05-19 PM (deep-review-driven next-steps plan locked into Â§22; Â§18.6 captures today's BOM-fix â†’ plugin install + Bucket B #5/#6 verification + voyage-style next-steps proposal from 4 parallel deep-think/deep-research/expert-coder/expert-coder-win11 agents; cuts and re-gates marked in Â§20; first task: Bucket F1 git-init aurora source)**\n4\t**Status:** Deployed and self-running. Nightly sweeps + publisher + morning briefing all firing on schedule via Windows Task Scheduler (verified: 5/17â†’5/18 sweeps at 05:00/06:00/07:00 UTC on time). KB at 335 artifacts, MTD spend $0.74/$60 caps. Gaps documented in Â§18 (extended in v4.1 to 22 items); integration work scoped in Â§19; re-prioritized punch list in Â§20; audit stamp in Â§21.\n5\t\n6\t**Change log from v1 â†’ v2**\n7\t- Applied the `deep-think` and `deep-research` skill protocols explicitly (see Â§0).\n8\t- Added **Templates** as a 4th artifact class caught by the Skills sweep (config templates, prompt templates, project scaffolds, document templates, agent templates like OpenClaw SOUL.md configs). Tagged with `kind='template'` in the schema; lighter-weight validation (no runner exec â€” they're not directly runnable).\n9\t- Promoted the **dual-axis** framing in Â§7 to be explicit: *what it does* Ã— *how complex a task it handles*. Both axes apply uniformly across all four artifact kinds.\n10\t- Added Â§15 â€” **Helping Hand**, a meta-skill that runs in any Cowork/Claude Code session and recommends from the KB. Default mode: approve-then-load. Skill + MCP server packaged together as `helping-hand.plugin`.\n11\t- Added Â§16 â€” **GitHub collaborator distribution**. Single private repo. Publisher stage commits scrubbed `kb-snapshot.sqlite` (no transcripts), full markdown library, and the latest `helping-hand.plugin` after each nightly cycle. Daily `YYYYMMDD` tags.\n12\t\n13\t**Change log v2 â†’ v3**\n14\t- All 10 Â§17 open questions resolved; decisions are committed and visible in Â§17 (renamed \"Decisions logged\").\n15\t- Added Â§9.4 â€” **08:30 morning briefing** as a Cowork scheduled session that consolidates the three exec summaries, surfaces budget, and renders PAT expiry reminders.\n16\t- Added **budget tracking** end-to-end: `costs` table in Â§6 schema, one-line budget block in every exec summary, full breakdown + 7-day trend + cap-projection warnings in the morning briefing. Dedicated Aurora-scoped Anthropic + Gemini keys with monthly caps ($50 / $10 to start).\n17\t- Added **PAT expiry surfacing** in the morning briefing (7/3/1 days); publisher hard-fails-loud on 401 with a `PAT_EXPIRED.txt` in the workspace folder.\n18\t- Set Aurora root to **`C:\\dev\\aurora\\`** (top-level, separate from this planning folder).\n19\t- Docker locked as the runner sandbox; Windows Task Scheduler locked as primary scheduler; Gemini locked as Critic B primary with a configurable local-LLM fallback.\n20\t\n21\t**Change log v3 â†’ v4 (post-launch reconciliation, 2026-05-18)**\n22\t- Added Â§18 (post-deployment status) â€” what's actually working vs. partial vs. gapped, including the overnight-outage incident and the hardening pass that followed.\n23\t- Added Â§19 (Ghost World Labs / OpenClaw integration scope) â€” non-executing sketch of how Helping Hand drops into GWL's GBrain-resolved OpenClaw agent stack. To be executed in a Cowork session opened inside `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`, not from this curator project.\n24\t- Added Â§20 (next-steps punch list) â€” 14 items prioritized by impact Ã— effort across this-week / 1-2-weeks / later. Includes sunburst, neural_plasticity populate, template-detection heuristic, dedicated keys, GWL integration, threshold calibration, P9 trigger.\n25\t- Documented hardening pass that wasn't in the v3 plan: publisher logging, launcher logging, missed-run watchdog, hybrid YAML parser, WakeToRun + StartWhenAvailable, Active Hours + 03:00 reboot pin, cross-runtime HH install, collaborator distribution.\n26\t- Factual corrections: Hermes star count (~95K, not 140K), GBrain storage (Postgres+pgvector with MCP *interface*, not \"MCP-based memory\"), OpenClaw governance (steering committee, not Steinberger).\n27\t- Added prompt-injection quarantine stage between scout and screener.\n28\t- Made critic independence structural, not aspirational â€” different input streams + at least one cross-vendor critic.\n29\t- GitHub dedupe rewritten around canonical normalization + aliases table.\n30\t- Reproducibility: per-run snapshots of seed maps, prompt templates, model IDs.\n31\t- Honest framing on the hyperbolic map (v1 = sunburst; learned-hyperbolic only at â‰¥500 artifacts).\n32\t- Sweep queueing with a global lock file.\n33\t- Interestingness decay added.\n34\t- Clone-don't-import isolation for license/legal hygiene.\n35\t- Seed maps expanded with verified additions (Letta v1, Mem0, MemoryAgentBench, official MCP Registry, Smithery, MCPfinder, awesome-claude-skills, claude-plugins.dev, Anthropic memory tool docs, Anthropic \"dreaming\" preview, Simon Willison's annotated system prompts).\n36\t- Neural-plasticity schema expanded with credit_assignment_latency, update_reversibility, interference_scope, memory_write_permissions, shipped_eval_harness.\n37\t- Velikov seed dropped (off-theme; bookmarked separately as methodology-watch).\n38\t- Top-K is now budget-derived, not a constant.\n39\t- Added prompt-state diff for in-prompt learners.\n40\t\n41\t---\n42\t\n43\t## Â§0 â€” Protocol applications (auditable)\n44\t\n45\t### 0.1 Deep-Think protocol applied (per `C:\\dev\\.claude\\skills\\deep-think\\SKILL.md`)\n46\t\n47\t**Deconstruction.** The plan in v1 made these load-bearing claims:\n48\t- C1: Scouts can be parallelized safely against the open web.\n49\t- C2: A two-critic + reconciler swarm produces independent judgments.\n50\t- C3: URL+content-hash dedupe is sufficient.\n51\t- C4: A hand-defined taxonomy + hashed-sibling-angle PoincarÃ© disk gives a meaningful hyperbolic embedding.\n52\t- C5: File-diff + DB-row inspection verifies \"what is modified\" claims for learning agents.\n53\t- C6: Scouts can grow their own seed map without runaway feedback.\n54\t- C7: K=5/5/3 is the right top-K split.\n55\t\n56\t**Multi-perspective.**\n57\t\n58\t*Happy path:* every sweep completes within budget, the static screener cuts noise to ~20%, the swarm scores the top-K honestly, the librarian writes clean rows, the exec summary surfaces 2â€“4 genuinely new items each night.\n59\t\n60\t*Failure modes I should have planned for and didn't:*"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3e5403d-da9f-4e88-817e-2103536b8c2e","uuid":"b94eaae2-0ab0-4b83-9bce-a7d546ad0579","timestamp":"2026-06-13T12:50:49.120Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md","content":"# Nightly Sweep Syst